.Dd 2026-06-16
.Dt NOMAD-MESH-BRIDGE 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm nomad-mesh-bridge
.Nd manage the USB Meshtastic serial-to-TCP bridge
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm nomad mesh-bridge
.Cm restart
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm nomad mesh-bridge
manages the
.Cm mesh-serial-bridge
LaunchAgent.
The bridge runs
.Xr socat 1
as a dumb pipe between the first USB-attached Meshtastic radio
.Pq Pa /dev/tty.{usbserial,usbmodem}*
and a
.Cm TCP-LISTEN
socket on port 4403, the Meshtastic default.
The containerised mesh stack and any LAN client can then reach a radio
the host owns.
.Pp
A full install already sets this up.
When no radio is attached the agent logs and exits cleanly; launchd's
.Cm KeepAlive
respawns it, so it reconnects the moment a radio appears.
.Sh COMMANDS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Cm restart
Boot out and re-bootstrap the bridge LaunchAgent in place.
If the agent is not yet installed, a full install of the bridge runs instead.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ~/Library/LaunchAgents/com.projectnomad.mesh-serial-bridge.plist
The LaunchAgent definition.
.It Pa ~/Library/Logs/nomad-mesh-serial-bridge.log
Bridge activity log (device detection, bind target).
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic nomad mesh-bridge restart
Restart the serial-to-TCP bridge after plugging in a radio.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr nomad 1 ,
.Xr nomad-install 1 ,
.Xr nomad-install-bridge 1 ,
.Xr nomad-reinstall 1
